WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:06.305 line:0%
(music)

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:12.345 line:0%
(music)

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:18.551 line:0%
(music)

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:25.524 line:0%
(music)

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:32.498 line:0%
(music)

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:39.472 line:0%
(music)

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:46.178 line:0%
(music)

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:53.085 line:0%
(music)

00:00:53.085 --> 00:01:00.059 line:0%
(music)

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:07.099 line:0%
(music)

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:14.073 line:0%
(music)

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:21.046 line:0%
(music)

00:01:21.046 --> 00:01:25.384 line:0%
(panting)

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:32.124 line:0%
(music)

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:38.798 line:0%
(music)

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:42.302 line:0%
<i> Nothing comes easy here</i>

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.770 line:0%
<i> in our wildest frontier.</i>

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:51.277 line:0%
(music)

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:54.581 line:0%
<i> Home to some of the deadliest
 animals on the planet.</i>

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.048 line:0%
(roar)

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.884 line:0%
(music)

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:00.886 line:0%
(bellows)

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:05.257 line:0%
(music)

00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:08.427 line:0%
<i> This is Alaska!</i>

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:11.764 line:0%
<i> And you need true grit
 to live here.</i>

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:19.338 line:0%
<i> North America doesn't get
 much colder nor any darker</i>

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:22.875 line:0%
<i> than Alaska in winter.</i>

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:26.312 line:0%
<i> The only way to survive here
 is to go wild.</i>

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.249 line:0%
(roaring)

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:35.188 line:0%
<i> This is a dangerous
 time of year.</i>

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:38.290 line:0%
<i> It's the end of winter.</i>

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:41.628 line:0%
<i> Competition for food
 is at its peak.</i>

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:48.601 line:0%
<i> This year's late arrival of
 spring heightens the tension.</i>

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:52.104 line:0%
<i> The hungry grow weaker.</i>

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:54.540 line:0%
<i> A golden eagle watches
 Steller's sea eagles</i>

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.910 line:0%
<i> arriving on his patch.</i>

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.850 line:0%
<i> They are not here to hunt;</i>

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.987 line:0%
<i> they're here to steal.</i>

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:10.756 line:0%
(squawking)

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:14.026 line:0%
<i> But a squabble breaks out
 within their gang.</i>

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:19.098 line:0%
<i> An opportunity for the golden
 eagle to win his food back.</i>

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:21.133 line:0%
<i> He's the bigger bird,</i>

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:24.670 line:0%
<i> and he's fully loaded
 with razor-sharp talons.</i>

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:30.343 line:0%
(music)

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:34.146 line:0%
<i> Talons that lock in
 the featherweight food fight.</i>

00:03:34.146 --> 00:03:38.417 line:0%
(music)

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:43.455 line:0%
(music)

00:03:43.455 --> 00:03:49.461 line:0%
(music)

00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:56.268 line:0%
(music)

00:03:56.268 --> 00:04:03.309 line:0%
(music)

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:10.282 line:0%
(music)

00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:17.256 line:0%
(music)

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:22.195 line:0%
<i> The battle rages...</i>

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:27.267 line:0%
<i> until the proud owner
 of this patch wins it back.</i>

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:35.507 line:0%
<i> Here in Alaska, only
 the toughest bird survives.</i>

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:38.811 line:0%
(music)

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:42.982 line:0%
<i> After months of punishing cold,
 it happens.</i>

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:48.854 line:0%
<i> Light breaks through
 the biggest sky in America.</i>

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:55.327 line:0%
(music)

00:04:55.327 --> 00:04:59.831 line:0%
<i> Warmth finally loosens
 winter's tight grip,</i>

00:04:59.831 --> 00:05:02.468 line:0%
<i> awakening new hungers.</i>

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.204 line:0%
<i> Alaska's north gets as many</i>

00:05:06.204 --> 00:05:11.210 line:0%
<i> as 40 additional minutes
 of light every day,</i>

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:14.447 line:0%
<i> until there's no night at all.</i>

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:23.289 line:0%
<i> Streams and rivers swell
 with melted ice and snow.</i>

00:05:25.557 --> 00:05:27.693 line:0%
<i> Animals that have
 struggled in winter</i>

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:29.862 line:0%
<i> now look for
 quick and easy meals</i>

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:32.365 line:0%
<i> brought by spring's abundance.</i>

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:40.440 line:0%
<i> But this is Alaska,
 where nothing is easy.</i>

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:44.443 line:0%
<i> Crabs lingering just
 below the tidal mark</i>

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:48.947 line:0%
<i> look like a trouble-free lunch
 for a mink.</i>

00:05:48.947 --> 00:05:55.287 line:0%
(music)

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:59.925 line:0%
<i> The mink is
 a specialized crab hunter.</i>

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:02.861 line:0%
<i> His teeth can easily
 crush shell.</i>

00:06:02.861 --> 00:06:09.068 line:0%
(music)

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:15.507 line:0%
(music)

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:22.481 line:0%
(music)

00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:29.455 line:0%
(music)

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:36.428 line:0%
(music)

00:06:36.428 --> 00:06:38.096 line:0%
<i> But the mink may have
 met his match</i>

00:06:38.096 --> 00:06:41.200 line:0%
<i> with this large Dungeness crab.</i>

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:47.372 line:0%
(music)

00:06:47.372 --> 00:06:54.346 line:0%
(music)

00:06:54.346 --> 00:07:01.386 line:0%
(music)

00:07:01.386 --> 00:07:07.960 line:0%
(music)

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:13.298 line:0%
<i> In Alaska sometimes the prey
 bites back...or pinches.</i>

00:07:13.298 --> 00:07:14.901 line:0%
(music)

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:17.570 line:0%
(squeaking)

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.439 line:0%
<i> So the mink has
 to get creative,</i>

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:25.277 line:0%
<i> taking out the enemy's
 defenses, limb by limb.</i>

00:07:25.277 --> 00:07:30.516 line:0%
(music)

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:34.553 line:0%
(music)

00:07:34.553 --> 00:07:39.692 line:0%
(music)

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:44.930 line:0%
<i> Even if the mink chews off all
 the legs, the crab might live.</i>

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.300 line:0%
<i> Legs grow back.</i>

00:07:51.236 --> 00:07:54.507 line:0%
(music)

00:07:54.507 --> 00:07:58.511 line:0%
<i> Top predators have a reputation
 for making lunch look easy.</i>

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:03.082 line:0%
<i> But they must contend
 with brilliant defenses</i>

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:05.451 line:0%
<i> conjured by said lunch.</i>

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:13.726 line:0%
<i> Exhibit A:
 a 20-pound porcupine.</i>

00:08:13.726 --> 00:08:17.295 line:0%
<i> Slow, subdued.</i>

00:08:17.295 --> 00:08:19.331 line:0%
<i> No doubt tasty.</i>

00:08:19.331 --> 00:08:26.305 line:0%
(music)

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:32.411 line:0%
(music)

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:38.450 line:0%
(music)

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:45.424 line:0%
(music)

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:49.395 line:0%
<i> But how to get by those
 nearly 30,000 quills?</i>

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:57.302 line:0%
<i> What the prey lacks in speed,
 it makes up for in defense.</i>

00:08:57.302 --> 00:08:59.938 line:0%
(panting)

00:08:59.938 --> 00:09:03.276 line:0%
<i> Each bacterium-filled quill
 can pierce the wolf's skin</i>

00:09:03.276 --> 00:09:05.944 line:0%
<i> like a hypodermic needle</i>

00:09:05.944 --> 00:09:09.549 line:0%
<i> and cause major infection.</i>

00:09:09.549 --> 00:09:11.917 line:0%
<i> A sharp reminder
 in these parts:</i>

00:09:11.917 --> 00:09:15.321 line:0%
<i> No meal is an easy meal.</i>

00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:23.995 line:0%
<i> The hunter decides the danger
 far outweighs the reward...</i>

00:09:23.995 --> 00:09:28.000 line:0%
<i> and moves on to something
 easier to swallow.</i>

00:09:45.083 --> 00:09:49.121 line:0%
<i> The now constant sunlight
 triggers tremendous growth.</i>

00:09:52.691 --> 00:09:55.927 line:0%
<i> The fertile grasses beckon
 great herds of caribou</i>

00:09:55.927 --> 00:09:58.897 line:0%
<i> here from colder
 Canadian plains.</i>

00:09:58.897 --> 00:10:04.169 line:0%
(music)

00:10:04.169 --> 00:10:08.441 line:0%
<i> A single herd can hold
 more than 120,000 caribou.</i>

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:17.549 line:0%
<i> During their annual migration</i>

00:10:17.549 --> 00:10:20.920 line:0%
<i> they'll cover
 more than 3,000 miles.</i>

00:10:27.193 --> 00:10:29.729 line:0%
<i> Their babies are often
 born on the move</i>

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:33.232 line:0%
<i> and need to to keep up
 with the herd.</i>

00:10:33.232 --> 00:10:37.269 line:0%
<i> One separated from the pack
 is a target.</i>

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:39.304 line:0%
(music)

00:10:39.304 --> 00:10:44.876 line:0%
(music)

00:10:44.876 --> 00:10:47.613 line:0%
<i> This calf has lost her way.</i>

00:10:50.683 --> 00:10:54.286 line:0%
<i> Just what the nearby hunters
 are banking on.</i>

00:10:54.286 --> 00:10:57.756 line:0%
(music)

00:10:57.756 --> 00:11:03.862 line:0%
(music)

00:11:03.862 --> 00:11:09.901 line:0%
(music)

00:11:09.901 --> 00:11:16.074 line:0%
(music)

00:11:16.074 --> 00:11:23.048 line:0%
(music)

00:11:23.048 --> 00:11:30.022 line:0%
(music)

00:11:30.022 --> 00:11:36.995 line:0%
(music)

00:11:36.995 --> 00:11:43.535 line:0%
(music)

00:11:43.535 --> 00:11:46.472 line:0%
<i> The calf escapes this time.</i>

00:11:46.472 --> 00:11:48.774 line:0%
<i> But another predator awaits...</i>

00:11:48.774 --> 00:11:52.144 line:0%
<i> more insidious
 and harder to shake.</i>

00:11:54.846 --> 00:11:58.684 line:0%
<i> Perhaps the deadliest
 animal of all.</i>

00:12:05.957 --> 00:12:11.230 line:0%
<i> Alaska's known for
 its jaws, paws and claws.</i>

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:15.901 line:0%
<i> But its smallest critter
 may be the biggest menace.</i>

00:12:15.901 --> 00:12:18.204 line:0%
<i> The mosquito.</i>

00:12:18.204 --> 00:12:23.109 line:0%
<i> More than 35 species feast
 in the endless daylight.</i>

00:12:24.676 --> 00:12:29.348 line:0%
<i> These mini-monsters lay dormant
 all winter as eggs.</i>

00:12:30.616 --> 00:12:34.986 line:0%
<i> Now the tundra underfoot
 turns to water,</i>

00:12:34.986 --> 00:12:37.656 line:0%
<i> triggering a mass hatching.</i>

00:12:37.656 --> 00:12:41.693 line:0%
(music)

00:12:41.693 --> 00:12:46.264 line:0%
<i> Just as caribou shed their
 winter coats, they attack.</i>

00:12:46.264 --> 00:12:50.770 line:0%
<i> If infection sets in, it could
 easily kill a baby caribou.</i>

00:12:53.238 --> 00:12:57.309 line:0%
<i> The mosquitoes then feast
 on festering wounds.</i>

00:12:57.309 --> 00:13:01.413 line:0%
(music)

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:04.283 line:0%
<i> Entire herds will reroute
 their migration</i>

00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:07.286 line:0%
<i> just to avoid
 the mosquito menace.</i>

00:13:10.789 --> 00:13:14.426 line:0%
<i> This group hugs the ocean
 and looks for a sea breeze</i>

00:13:14.426 --> 00:13:17.362 line:0%
<i> to blow the buzzing
 from their backs.</i>

00:13:17.362 --> 00:13:21.500 line:0%
(music)

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:27.539 line:0%
(music)

00:13:27.539 --> 00:13:34.179 line:0%
(music)

00:13:34.179 --> 00:13:38.683 line:0%
<i> There's little relief, even
 standing in the Arctic Ocean.</i>

00:13:38.683 --> 00:13:45.657 line:0%
(buzzing)

00:13:45.657 --> 00:13:52.631 line:0%
(buzzing)

00:13:52.631 --> 00:13:59.271 line:0%
(buzzing)

00:13:59.271 --> 00:14:04.142 line:0%
<i> Never has such a deadly
 creature been just so annoying.</i>

00:14:04.142 --> 00:14:09.648 line:0%
(music)

00:14:09.648 --> 00:14:14.786 line:0%
<i> There's nothing left to do but
 plunge into a full-body bath,</i>

00:14:14.786 --> 00:14:17.122 line:0%
<i> which seems to do the trick.</i>

00:14:17.122 --> 00:14:23.728 line:0%
(music)

00:14:23.728 --> 00:14:27.867 line:0%
<i> No animal is immune to
 its bloodsucking attacks.</i>

00:14:29.701 --> 00:14:34.105 line:0%
<i> And as quickly as they
 appeared, they vanish.</i>

00:14:34.105 --> 00:14:39.544 line:0%
(music)

00:14:39.544 --> 00:14:40.846 line:0%
<i> Plentiful water brings</i>

00:14:40.846 --> 00:14:44.649 line:0%
<i> a different kind of horde
 to Alaska.</i>

00:14:44.649 --> 00:14:48.953 line:0%
(music)

00:14:48.953 --> 00:14:51.323 line:0%
(tinkling)

00:14:51.323 --> 00:14:55.794 line:0%
<i> The streams and rivers swell
 with melted ice and snow.</i>

00:14:55.794 --> 00:15:00.165 line:0%
<i> By late spring,
 the waterways gush.</i>

00:15:00.165 --> 00:15:03.468 line:0%
<i> Sockeye salmon arrive
 from the Pacific.</i>

00:15:03.468 --> 00:15:07.906 line:0%
(music)

00:15:07.906 --> 00:15:10.342 line:0%
<i> Over 30 million of them,</i>

00:15:10.342 --> 00:15:14.879 line:0%
<i> swimming upriver to spawn in
 the very place they were born.</i>

00:15:14.879 --> 00:15:18.650 line:0%
(music)

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:22.987 line:0%
<i> Of the thousands that arrive,
 only a few make it back.</i>

00:15:22.987 --> 00:15:25.924 line:0%
<i> They've got a lot of obstacles
 on their way up--</i>

00:15:25.924 --> 00:15:29.561 line:0%
<i> dams, disease, fishermen.</i>

00:15:34.165 --> 00:15:39.037 line:0%
<i> But the last thing they want
 to encounter is this guy.</i>

00:15:39.037 --> 00:15:40.705 line:0%
<i> The brown bear.</i>

00:15:40.705 --> 00:15:42.774 line:0%
<i> The ultimate predator.</i>

00:15:42.774 --> 00:15:45.144 line:0%
(roaring)

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:51.550 line:0%
<i> Adult males sport four-inch
 non-retractable claws</i>

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.786 line:0%
<i> that can slash with precision.</i>

00:15:55.687 --> 00:15:58.390 line:0%
<i> They have three-inch
 canine teeth</i>

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.826 line:0%
<i> that grasp and tear flesh.</i>

00:16:03.562 --> 00:16:08.433 line:0%
<i> Brown bears are among the
 strongest creatures on Earth.</i>

00:16:08.433 --> 00:16:11.669 line:0%
<i> And strength needs fuel...</i>

00:16:11.669 --> 00:16:13.872 line:0%
<i> lots of it.</i>

00:16:17.575 --> 00:16:22.348 line:0%
<i> After months of slim pickings,
 it's time for a fish feast.</i>

00:16:26.718 --> 00:16:30.488 line:0%
<i> These bears need
 a protein boost, fast.</i>

00:16:30.488 --> 00:16:33.792 line:0%
(music)

00:16:33.792 --> 00:16:37.762 line:0%
(music)

00:16:37.762 --> 00:16:40.699 line:0%
<i> This is where rank
 in brown bear hierarchy</i>

00:16:40.699 --> 00:16:43.501 line:0%
<i> matters most.</i>

00:16:43.501 --> 00:16:46.338 line:0%
<i> A rocky outcrop, midway across,</i>

00:16:46.338 --> 00:16:50.442 line:0%
<i> is one of the best fishing
 positions on the river.</i>

00:16:52.377 --> 00:16:57.349 line:0%
<i> Control of this perch gives
 its owner a critical advantage.</i>

00:16:57.349 --> 00:17:02.087 line:0%
(music)

00:17:02.087 --> 00:17:09.060 line:0%
(music)

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:15.567 line:0%
(music)

00:17:15.567 --> 00:17:19.738 line:0%
<i> Here, fishing requires
 virtually no effort.</i>

00:17:19.738 --> 00:17:23.408 line:0%
(music)

00:17:23.408 --> 00:17:25.277 line:0%
<i> It's possible to pack on pounds</i>

00:17:25.277 --> 00:17:29.114 line:0%
<i> and save energy
 at the same time.</i>

00:17:29.114 --> 00:17:31.349 line:0%
(music)

00:17:31.349 --> 00:17:36.388 line:0%
(music)

00:17:36.388 --> 00:17:42.627 line:0%
(music)

00:17:42.627 --> 00:17:45.664 line:0%
<i> Downstream, a mother bear
 and her cubs</i>

00:17:45.664 --> 00:17:48.032 line:0%
<i> approach the good spot.</i>

00:17:48.032 --> 00:17:51.736 line:0%
(music)

00:17:51.736 --> 00:17:58.277 line:0%
(music)

00:17:58.277 --> 00:18:02.114 line:0%
<i> The growing cubs
 need the protein,</i>

00:18:02.114 --> 00:18:05.483 line:0%
<i> but this is a dangerous place
 for them.</i>

00:18:05.483 --> 00:18:07.519 line:0%
(music)

00:18:07.519 --> 00:18:12.858 line:0%
(music)

00:18:12.858 --> 00:18:16.995 line:0%
<i> Aggressive males can injure
 or even kill them.</i>

00:18:16.995 --> 00:18:19.030 line:0%
(music)

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:25.937 line:0%
(music)

00:18:25.937 --> 00:18:32.143 line:0%
(music)

00:18:32.143 --> 00:18:36.181 line:0%
<i> The swift current separates
 the mother from her young.</i>

00:18:36.181 --> 00:18:39.484 line:0%
(squawking)

00:18:39.484 --> 00:18:41.519 line:0%
(music)

00:18:41.519 --> 00:18:48.459 line:0%
(music)

00:18:48.459 --> 00:18:52.397 line:0%
<i> An older male seizes
 his opportunity...</i>

00:18:52.397 --> 00:18:53.665 line:0%
<i> and attacks.</i>

00:18:53.665 --> 00:18:59.637 line:0%
(music)

00:18:59.637 --> 00:19:03.308 line:0%
<i> He could easily
 slaughter the cubs.</i>

00:19:03.308 --> 00:19:06.411 line:0%
<i> But mother steps in.</i>

00:19:06.411 --> 00:19:11.650 line:0%
(roaring)

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:16.855 line:0%
<i> At this moment, she may be the
 most dangerous bear in Alaska.</i>

00:19:19.123 --> 00:19:22.928 line:0%
<i> The older male outweighs her
 by 500 pounds.</i>

00:19:24.496 --> 00:19:25.864 line:0%
(roar)

00:19:25.864 --> 00:19:29.902 line:0%
<i> But he knows not to mess
 with a mother's fury.</i>

00:19:32.136 --> 00:19:37.742 line:0%
<i> And he has more important
 things to worry about,</i>

00:19:37.742 --> 00:19:42.080 line:0%
<i> like maintaining his position
 above the falls.</i>

00:19:49.587 --> 00:19:50.922 line:0%
<i> During the fight,</i>

00:19:50.922 --> 00:19:54.493 line:0%
<i> the older male lost
 his prized fishing spot.</i>

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:01.032 line:0%
<i> Young challengers have
 seized the opportunity</i>

00:20:01.032 --> 00:20:03.835 line:0%
<i> and moved in on his turf.</i>

00:20:03.835 --> 00:20:10.108 line:0%
(music)

00:20:10.108 --> 00:20:16.381 line:0%
(music)

00:20:16.381 --> 00:20:23.354 line:0%
(music)

00:20:23.354 --> 00:20:30.328 line:0%
(music)

00:20:30.328 --> 00:20:37.302 line:0%
(music)

00:20:37.302 --> 00:20:41.840 line:0%
<i> Now, the balance of power
 teeters above the falls.</i>

00:20:44.276 --> 00:20:46.478 line:0%
<i> The older bear
 has more experience</i>

00:20:46.478 --> 00:20:49.013 line:0%
<i> but is weakened
 by his fighting.</i>

00:20:49.013 --> 00:20:51.049 line:0%
(music)

00:20:51.049 --> 00:20:56.221 line:0%
(music)

00:20:56.221 --> 00:20:58.557 line:0%
(roar)

00:20:58.557 --> 00:21:02.127 line:0%
<i> This younger, stronger rival
 seizes his chance</i>

00:21:02.127 --> 00:21:04.162 line:0%
<i> to oust the older bear.</i>

00:21:04.162 --> 00:21:09.233 line:0%
(roaring)

00:21:09.233 --> 00:21:12.236 line:0%
(music)

00:21:12.236 --> 00:21:18.844 line:0%
(music)

00:21:18.844 --> 00:21:20.645 line:0%
(roar)

00:21:20.645 --> 00:21:26.918 line:0%
(music)

00:21:26.918 --> 00:21:32.957 line:0%
(music)

00:21:32.957 --> 00:21:38.963 line:0%
(music)

00:21:38.963 --> 00:21:42.433 line:0%
(roaring)

00:21:42.433 --> 00:21:46.037 line:0%
(music)

00:21:46.037 --> 00:21:50.108 line:0%
<i> The fallen king is chased
 further downstream.</i>

00:21:50.108 --> 00:21:54.078 line:0%
(music)

00:21:54.078 --> 00:21:57.082 line:0%
<i> A loss of rank could mean
 the loss of life,</i>

00:21:57.082 --> 00:21:59.951 line:0%
<i> especially during
 the salmon run,</i>

00:21:59.951 --> 00:22:04.189 line:0%
<i> when the window of opportunity
 will soon abruptly shut.</i>

00:22:07.892 --> 00:22:10.395 line:0%
<i> Such is the hardship
 for Alaskan predators</i>

00:22:10.395 --> 00:22:14.232 line:0%
<i> whose warm weather bounty lasts
 but a blink of an eye.</i>

00:22:17.468 --> 00:22:20.305 line:0%
<i> The Arctic fox is looking
 forward to summer,</i>

00:22:20.305 --> 00:22:22.740 line:0%
<i> however brief.</i>

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:27.311 line:0%
<i> His icy wasteland transforms
 into a land of possibilities.</i>

00:22:27.311 --> 00:22:33.184 line:0%
(music)

00:22:33.184 --> 00:22:35.787 line:0%
<i> All requiring stealth.</i>

00:22:35.787 --> 00:22:41.059 line:0%
(music)

00:22:41.059 --> 00:22:44.962 line:0%
<i> Step one: a new wardrobe.</i>

00:22:44.962 --> 00:22:50.301 line:0%
<i> Get rid of the white winter fur
 coat to match the new terrain.</i>

00:22:50.301 --> 00:22:56.207 line:0%
<i> Now he's an expert
 at hiding in plain sight.</i>

00:22:56.207 --> 00:22:59.043 line:0%
<i> The goal is to catch
 most of a year's prey</i>

00:22:59.043 --> 00:23:01.712 line:0%
<i> in a very short window of time.</i>

00:23:01.712 --> 00:23:03.047 line:0%
(howling)

00:23:03.047 --> 00:23:05.584 line:0%
<i> It will make or break him.</i>

00:23:08.653 --> 00:23:12.757 line:0%
<i> Suddenly, a feast arrives.</i>

00:23:12.757 --> 00:23:14.959 line:0%
<i> Millions of migratory birds</i>

00:23:14.959 --> 00:23:18.329 line:0%
<i> turn his island
 into an Easter basket.</i>

00:23:18.329 --> 00:23:25.136 line:0%
(music)

00:23:25.136 --> 00:23:32.076 line:0%
(music)

00:23:32.076 --> 00:23:38.082 line:0%
(music)

00:23:38.082 --> 00:23:42.086 line:0%
<i> One lost egg tastes good.</i>

00:23:42.086 --> 00:23:44.756 line:0%
<i> Imagine a whole nest.</i>

00:23:44.756 --> 00:23:51.262 line:0%
(music)

00:23:51.262 --> 00:23:54.665 line:0%
<i> But getting at the mother lode
 can be tricky.</i>

00:23:54.665 --> 00:23:58.035 line:0%
<i> Because of, well, mothers...</i>

00:23:58.035 --> 00:23:59.904 line:0%
<i> and fathers.</i>

00:23:59.904 --> 00:24:02.006 line:0%
(music)

00:24:02.006 --> 00:24:08.480 line:0%
(music)

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:14.152 line:0%
(squawking)

00:24:14.152 --> 00:24:17.488 line:0%
<i> Arctic terns are
 fearless parents.</i>

00:24:17.488 --> 00:24:19.524 line:0%
(music)

00:24:19.524 --> 00:24:24.795 line:0%
(music)

00:24:24.795 --> 00:24:27.331 line:0%
(cheeping)

00:24:27.331 --> 00:24:29.367 line:0%
<i> These birds can draw blood.</i>

00:24:29.367 --> 00:24:33.338 line:0%
(music)

00:24:33.338 --> 00:24:36.908 line:0%
(squawking)

00:24:36.908 --> 00:24:39.610 line:0%
<i> And they'll even
 peck out his eyes.</i>

00:24:39.610 --> 00:24:44.382 line:0%
(music)

00:24:44.382 --> 00:24:47.985 line:0%
<i> The Arctic fox
 dodges his attackers.</i>

00:24:47.985 --> 00:24:51.889 line:0%
<i> But he still needs to meet
 a huge quota of prey.</i>

00:24:51.889 --> 00:24:55.893 line:0%
(music)

00:24:55.893 --> 00:24:58.930 line:0%
<i> He's hunting for six.</i>

00:24:58.930 --> 00:25:03.502 line:0%
<i> So he avoids the vigilantly
 protected nest all together.</i>

00:25:06.805 --> 00:25:09.207 line:0%
<i> And goes right for the chick.</i>

00:25:11.676 --> 00:25:16.414 line:0%
<i> A bird in the mouth is worth
 at least a dozen eggs.</i>

00:25:19.751 --> 00:25:22.486 line:0%
<i> Another predator that stalks
 these barren lands</i>

00:25:22.486 --> 00:25:27.558 line:0%
<i> is 100 times larger
 than the fox</i>

00:25:27.558 --> 00:25:29.660 line:0%
<i> with an appetite to match.</i>

00:25:29.660 --> 00:25:34.766 line:0%
(music)

00:25:34.766 --> 00:25:37.034 line:0%
<i> And unlike
 her brown bear cousins,</i>

00:25:37.034 --> 00:25:39.370 line:0%
<i> polar bears don't hibernate,</i>

00:25:39.370 --> 00:25:41.673 line:0%
<i> they hunt year-round.</i>

00:25:45.276 --> 00:25:49.981 line:0%
<i> In winter, polar bears eat
 seals that live on the ice.</i>

00:25:49.981 --> 00:25:53.117 line:0%
(music)

00:25:53.117 --> 00:25:58.155 line:0%
(music)

00:25:58.155 --> 00:26:04.963 line:0%
(music)

00:26:04.963 --> 00:26:10.368 line:0%
<i> But come spring,
 they are nowhere to be found.</i>

00:26:11.936 --> 00:26:16.808 line:0%
<i> So, she must go far and wide
 to find something to eat.</i>

00:26:24.215 --> 00:26:26.384 line:0%
<i> A polar bear's search for food</i>

00:26:26.384 --> 00:26:29.820 line:0%
<i> is even harder
 in a warming climate.</i>

00:26:29.820 --> 00:26:34.525 line:0%
<i> The farther she must swim,
 the hungrier she gets.</i>

00:26:34.525 --> 00:26:38.630 line:0%
(music)

00:26:38.630 --> 00:26:41.966 line:0%
<i> A lucky break
 for the polar bear.</i>

00:26:41.966 --> 00:26:45.937 line:0%
<i> The sea has done
 her work for her.</i>

00:26:45.937 --> 00:26:48.706 line:0%
<i> A washed-up whale carcass.</i>

00:26:48.706 --> 00:26:53.444 line:0%
<i> It's an amazing sight:
 27 tons of blubber.</i>

00:26:53.444 --> 00:26:57.782 line:0%
(music)

00:26:57.782 --> 00:27:04.055 line:0%
(music)

00:27:04.055 --> 00:27:07.025 line:0%
(squawking)

00:27:07.025 --> 00:27:10.662 line:0%
<i> It's an all-you-can-eat
 blubber buffet</i>

00:27:10.662 --> 00:27:14.599 line:0%
<i> and her first bite of
 substantial food in months.</i>

00:27:17.568 --> 00:27:22.039 line:0%
<i> Amazingly, it could feed her
 for a whole year.</i>

00:27:22.039 --> 00:27:25.510 line:0%
<i> But that's if she
 has it to herself.</i>

00:27:27.111 --> 00:27:30.281 line:0%
<i> Other ice bears have
 the same idea.</i>

00:27:30.281 --> 00:27:33.317 line:0%
(music)

00:27:33.317 --> 00:27:39.357 line:0%
(music)

00:27:39.357 --> 00:27:42.427 line:0%
<i> The small bears
 are enthusiastic.</i>

00:27:44.428 --> 00:27:48.799 line:0%
<i> They're still nursing, but
 also need their fill of fat.</i>

00:27:48.799 --> 00:27:52.003 line:0%
(music)

00:27:52.003 --> 00:27:58.543 line:0%
(music)

00:27:58.543 --> 00:28:03.081 line:0%
<i> And suddenly,
 a huge male appears.</i>

00:28:03.081 --> 00:28:07.551 line:0%
<i> His hunger is
 as big as his bark.</i>

00:28:07.551 --> 00:28:10.855 line:0%
(grunting)

00:28:10.855 --> 00:28:16.928 line:0%
<i> A smaller mother bear isn't
 happy about the intrusion...</i>

00:28:16.928 --> 00:28:20.364 line:0%
<i> and tries to teach him
 a lesson.</i>

00:28:20.364 --> 00:28:24.335 line:0%
(roaring)

00:28:24.335 --> 00:28:30.808 line:0%
(music)

00:28:30.808 --> 00:28:35.413 line:0%
(grunting)

00:28:35.413 --> 00:28:41.886 line:0%
(music)

00:28:41.886 --> 00:28:48.192 line:0%
(music)

00:28:48.192 --> 00:28:54.232 line:0%
(birds squawking)

00:28:54.232 --> 00:29:00.271 line:0%
(birds squawking)

00:29:00.271 --> 00:29:03.474 line:0%
<i> He sneaks in
 from another angle.</i>

00:29:03.474 --> 00:29:06.377 line:0%
<i> But he's told to wait his turn.</i>

00:29:06.377 --> 00:29:09.980 line:0%
(panting)

00:29:09.980 --> 00:29:12.249 line:0%
<i> Once the others
 have had their fill,</i>

00:29:12.249 --> 00:29:16.554 line:0%
<i> the male is finally given
 permission to lick the fat.</i>

00:29:28.332 --> 00:29:34.305 line:0%
<i> After months of summer, the
 sunshine is no longer endless.</i>

00:29:34.305 --> 00:29:38.509 line:0%
<i> And chilly, misty mornings
 mark the arrival of autumn</i>

00:29:38.509 --> 00:29:41.246 line:0%
<i> and the return of giants.</i>

00:29:44.615 --> 00:29:49.153 line:0%
<i> A moose bull in his prime
 shows off his splendid antlers.</i>

00:29:49.153 --> 00:29:56.161 line:0%
(music)

00:29:56.161 --> 00:29:58.796 line:0%
<i> He jousts loudly
 with vegetation</i>

00:29:58.796 --> 00:30:02.766 line:0%
<i> for the benefit of cows
 and fellow bulls alike.</i>

00:30:02.766 --> 00:30:07.104 line:0%
(rustling)

00:30:07.104 --> 00:30:09.807 line:0%
<i> The biggest racks actually
 make a different sound</i>

00:30:09.807 --> 00:30:11.776 line:0%
<i> than the smaller ones,</i>

00:30:11.776 --> 00:30:16.581 line:0%
<i> announcing size and status to
 anyone who might be listening.</i>

00:30:19.050 --> 00:30:22.120 line:0%
<i> The females take notice.</i>

00:30:27.591 --> 00:30:29.794 line:0%
<i> Other bulls
 entering their prime</i>

00:30:29.794 --> 00:30:32.563 line:0%
<i> and bearing equally
 impressive headgear</i>

00:30:32.563 --> 00:30:35.065 line:0%
<i> are drawn to
 the scent of the cows.</i>

00:30:35.065 --> 00:30:39.437 line:0%
(music)

00:30:39.437 --> 00:30:43.073 line:0%
<i> The stage is awash
 in testosterone,</i>

00:30:43.073 --> 00:30:46.644 line:0%
<i> and trouble can't be
 far behind.</i>

00:30:49.180 --> 00:30:52.082 line:0%
<i> The bulls are ready to rumble.</i>

00:30:52.082 --> 00:30:54.118 line:0%
(music)

00:30:54.118 --> 00:30:59.390 line:0%
(music)

00:31:04.628 --> 00:31:06.764 line:0%
<i> With the rut in full swing,</i>

00:31:06.764 --> 00:31:09.199 line:0%
<i> a come-hither look
 from a moose cow</i>

00:31:09.199 --> 00:31:11.569 line:0%
<i> brings the dominant bull
 running.</i>

00:31:11.569 --> 00:31:16.607 line:0%
(music)

00:31:16.607 --> 00:31:19.910 line:0%
<i> The females are getting
 more and more receptive,</i>

00:31:19.910 --> 00:31:22.779 line:0%
<i> showing their approval
 of the big bull's status</i>

00:31:22.779 --> 00:31:25.316 line:0%
<i> by contributing their
 pheromone-laden urine</i>

00:31:25.316 --> 00:31:27.351 line:0%
<i> to his rut pits.</i>

00:31:27.351 --> 00:31:33.390 line:0%
(music)

00:31:33.390 --> 00:31:39.463 line:0%
(music)

00:31:39.463 --> 00:31:42.032 line:0%
<i> With his exquisitely
 sensitive nose,</i>

00:31:42.032 --> 00:31:44.969 line:0%
<i> he checks on a cow's readiness.</i>

00:31:47.038 --> 00:31:50.975 line:0%
<i> He seems pleased
 with the results.</i>

00:31:50.975 --> 00:31:53.444 line:0%
(groans)

00:31:53.444 --> 00:31:59.116 line:0%
<i> At 11 years old, he is truly a
 picture of a bull in his prime.</i>

00:31:59.116 --> 00:32:05.422 line:0%
<i> 1,500 pounds, seven feet high
 at the shoulder,</i>

00:32:05.422 --> 00:32:08.126 line:0%
<i> with a six-foot rack.</i>

00:32:10.194 --> 00:32:13.631 line:0%
<i> It's no wonder the cows
 like what they see!</i>

00:32:16.700 --> 00:32:20.003 line:0%
<i> But there's trouble
 on the horizon.</i>

00:32:20.003 --> 00:32:23.707 line:0%
<i> A younger and equally
 impressive bull.</i>

00:32:23.707 --> 00:32:28.312 line:0%
(music)

00:32:28.312 --> 00:32:31.048 line:0%
<i> The challenger approaches,</i>

00:32:31.048 --> 00:32:35.019 line:0%
<i> waving his great antlers
 from side to side.</i>

00:32:37.822 --> 00:32:40.591 line:0%
<i> The master responds.</i>

00:32:43.927 --> 00:32:46.964 line:0%
<i> These rituals of intimidation
 are usually enough</i>

00:32:46.964 --> 00:32:49.867 line:0%
<i> to determine who will dominate,</i>

00:32:49.867 --> 00:32:53.737 line:0%
<i> thus avoiding the risk
 of injury in a fight.</i>

00:32:53.737 --> 00:33:00.544 line:0%
(music)

00:33:00.544 --> 00:33:04.448 line:0%
<i> The females have a keen
 interest in the outcome.</i>

00:33:04.448 --> 00:33:06.483 line:0%
(music)

00:33:06.483 --> 00:33:11.655 line:0%
(music)

00:33:11.655 --> 00:33:15.659 line:0%
<i> Like prize fighters,
 they stare each other down,</i>

00:33:15.659 --> 00:33:19.998 line:0%
<i> circle and wait for an opening.</i>

00:33:22.900 --> 00:33:25.436 line:0%
<i> Neither is backing down.</i>

00:33:25.436 --> 00:33:28.339 line:0%
(music)

00:33:28.339 --> 00:33:34.144 line:0%
(clattering)

00:33:34.144 --> 00:33:37.915 line:0%
(music)

00:33:37.915 --> 00:33:39.817 line:0%
<i> With equally matched bulls,</i>

00:33:39.817 --> 00:33:43.287 line:0%
<i> the battle may last
 up to a half an hour or more.</i>

00:33:43.287 --> 00:33:44.888 line:0%
(music)

00:33:44.888 --> 00:33:51.862 line:0%
(music)

00:33:51.862 --> 00:33:55.500 line:0%
<i> But the older bull soon
 gains the upper hand.</i>

00:33:57.635 --> 00:34:02.072 line:0%
<i> He batters the challenger
 unmercifully.</i>

00:34:02.072 --> 00:34:03.741 line:0%
(bellows)

00:34:03.741 --> 00:34:08.212 line:0%
(music)

00:34:08.212 --> 00:34:14.652 line:0%
(music)

00:34:14.652 --> 00:34:18.556 line:0%
<i> Abruptly,
 the contest is decided.</i>

00:34:21.258 --> 00:34:24.762 line:0%
<i> The master will return
 to his harem.</i>

00:34:27.598 --> 00:34:31.903 line:0%
<i> The younger one paid the price
 for his bid to reproduce.</i>

00:34:33.470 --> 00:34:39.977 line:0%
<i> In this unforgiving place,
 his wounded leg may spell doom.</i>

00:34:47.050 --> 00:34:50.954 line:0%
<i> The victor has urgent business
 to tend to.</i>

00:34:50.954 --> 00:34:57.561 line:0%
(music)

00:34:57.561 --> 00:35:01.165 line:0%
<i> And just in time.</i>

00:35:01.165 --> 00:35:04.168 line:0%
<i> Fall is on the way out.</i>

00:35:06.871 --> 00:35:09.406 line:0%
<i> Winter comes early this year.</i>

00:35:09.406 --> 00:35:11.942 line:0%
(music)

00:35:11.942 --> 00:35:18.248 line:0%
(music)

00:35:18.248 --> 00:35:23.954 line:0%
<i> Record snowfall gives
 deep cover for rodents...</i>

00:35:23.954 --> 00:35:25.823 line:0%
<i> like the vole.</i>

00:35:25.823 --> 00:35:32.029 line:0%
(music)

00:35:32.029 --> 00:35:38.068 line:0%
(music)

00:35:38.068 --> 00:35:44.941 line:0%
(music)

00:35:44.941 --> 00:35:47.711 line:0%
<i> Hidden beneath, they are
 protected from the cold</i>

00:35:47.711 --> 00:35:49.680 line:0%
<i> and hunters above.</i>

00:35:49.680 --> 00:35:53.784 line:0%
(music)

00:35:53.784 --> 00:35:56.019 line:0%
(music)

00:35:56.019 --> 00:35:57.454 line:0%
(squeak)

00:35:57.454 --> 00:36:01.024 line:0%
(music)

00:36:01.024 --> 00:36:05.228 line:0%
(music)

00:36:05.228 --> 00:36:09.367 line:0%
<i> The vole's ears are big and
 can listen out for danger.</i>

00:36:13.370 --> 00:36:18.308 line:0%
<i> But what good is that
 if danger makes no sound?</i>

00:36:18.308 --> 00:36:23.514 line:0%
(music)

00:36:23.514 --> 00:36:27.484 line:0%
<i> Silence is the snowy owl's
 secret weapon.</i>

00:36:27.484 --> 00:36:29.586 line:0%
(music)

00:36:29.586 --> 00:36:35.192 line:0%
(music)

00:36:35.192 --> 00:36:37.527 line:0%
<i> Fringed edges of
 her flight feathers</i>

00:36:37.527 --> 00:36:41.465 line:0%
<i> break up the flapping noise
 that a normal bird makes.</i>

00:36:41.465 --> 00:36:47.405 line:0%
(music)

00:36:47.405 --> 00:36:51.475 line:0%
<i> And her attack
 is as silent as death.</i>

00:36:51.475 --> 00:36:56.247 line:0%
(music)

00:36:56.247 --> 00:36:59.116 line:0%
<i> The vole never knew
 what hit him.</i>

00:36:59.116 --> 00:37:03.387 line:0%
(music)

00:37:03.387 --> 00:37:09.426 line:0%
(music)

00:37:09.426 --> 00:37:16.033 line:0%
(music)

00:37:16.033 --> 00:37:19.503 line:0%
<i> Snow is a problem
 for predator and prey alike,</i>

00:37:19.503 --> 00:37:22.673 line:0%
<i> mostly because it makes sound.</i>

00:37:25.008 --> 00:37:29.513 line:0%
<i> But Alaska's creature have come
 up with ingenious workarounds.</i>

00:37:29.513 --> 00:37:31.548 line:0%
(music)

00:37:31.548 --> 00:37:37.454 line:0%
(music)

00:37:37.454 --> 00:37:42.793 line:0%
<i> The red fox has perfected
 the hunt below and above.</i>

00:37:42.793 --> 00:37:44.828 line:0%
(music)

00:37:44.828 --> 00:37:50.401 line:0%
(music)

00:37:50.401 --> 00:37:54.705 line:0%
<i> At only 10 pounds, he doesn't
 break the snow's surface.</i>

00:37:54.705 --> 00:37:57.975 line:0%
(music)

00:37:57.975 --> 00:38:04.881 line:0%
(music)

00:38:04.881 --> 00:38:09.787 line:0%
<i> So he can search for prey
 without detection.</i>

00:38:11.355 --> 00:38:16.059 line:0%
<i> But his prey hides
 below the surface.</i>

00:38:16.059 --> 00:38:19.130 line:0%
<i> So how do you find
 what you cannot see?</i>

00:38:26.570 --> 00:38:31.141 line:0%
<i> Big ears and magnetic senses.</i>

00:38:31.141 --> 00:38:34.111 line:0%
<i> Synced together,
 these secret weapons</i>

00:38:34.111 --> 00:38:37.748 line:0%
<i> make the red fox
 a stealth hunter,</i>

00:38:37.748 --> 00:38:43.320 line:0%
<i> able to catch his victims
 under nearly two feet of snow.</i>

00:38:43.320 --> 00:38:47.058 line:0%
<i> First he pinpoints
 the faintest sound.</i>

00:38:59.970 --> 00:39:04.775 line:0%
<i> Then homes in on the sweet spot
 where the angle of the sound</i>

00:39:04.775 --> 00:39:09.446 line:0%
<i> matches the slope of
 the planet's magnetic field.</i>

00:39:09.446 --> 00:39:12.549 line:0%
<i> Once the fox locks on
 to that spot,</i>

00:39:12.549 --> 00:39:16.153 line:0%
<i> he can calculate the exact
 distance to his prey.</i>

00:39:17.754 --> 00:39:20.658 line:0%
<i> In this case, a meadow vole.</i>

00:39:23.760 --> 00:39:25.662 line:0%
<i> But then what?</i>

00:39:25.662 --> 00:39:28.231 line:0%
(music)

00:39:28.231 --> 00:39:32.569 line:0%
(rustling)

00:39:32.569 --> 00:39:36.373 line:0%
<i> If he digs, the vole will flee.</i>

00:39:36.373 --> 00:39:39.476 line:0%
(rustling)

00:39:39.476 --> 00:39:43.613 line:0%
<i> So instead, he flies.</i>

00:39:43.613 --> 00:39:48.652 line:0%
(music)

00:39:48.652 --> 00:39:55.058 line:0%
(music)

00:39:55.058 --> 00:40:02.032 line:0%
(music)

00:40:02.032 --> 00:40:04.968 line:0%
(music)

00:40:04.968 --> 00:40:08.939 line:0%
(sniffing)

00:40:08.939 --> 00:40:15.912 line:0%
(music)

00:40:15.912 --> 00:40:22.886 line:0%
(music)

00:40:22.886 --> 00:40:28.391 line:0%
(music)

00:40:28.391 --> 00:40:33.563 line:0%
(snarling)

00:40:33.563 --> 00:40:36.266 line:0%
(music)

00:40:36.266 --> 00:40:39.336 line:0%
<i> A small bite,</i>

00:40:39.336 --> 00:40:42.773 line:0%
<i> but in winter
 every calorie counts.</i>

00:40:48.279 --> 00:40:51.048 line:0%
<i> Alaska's snows inspire
 a million ways</i>

00:40:51.048 --> 00:40:53.417 line:0%
<i> for hunters to innovate.</i>

00:40:55.752 --> 00:41:00.023 line:0%
<i> One of those ways is to
 stop hunting altogether.</i>

00:41:00.023 --> 00:41:02.593 line:0%
<i> And start scavenging.</i>

00:41:04.161 --> 00:41:06.963 line:0%
<i> The wolverine's nose
 leads the way,</i>

00:41:06.963 --> 00:41:09.900 line:0%
<i> sniffing out prey
 and hibernating animals</i>

00:41:09.900 --> 00:41:13.403 line:0%
<i> buried more than 20 feet
 beneath the snow.</i>

00:41:13.403 --> 00:41:18.975 line:0%
(music)

00:41:18.975 --> 00:41:25.415 line:0%
(music)

00:41:25.415 --> 00:41:28.485 line:0%
<i> This dog-sized weasel
 is able to take down</i>

00:41:28.485 --> 00:41:30.387 line:0%
<i> a full-grown caribou.</i>

00:41:32.489 --> 00:41:36.893 line:0%
<i> But today, this wolverine
 is saving his energy.</i>

00:41:36.893 --> 00:41:39.396 line:0%
<i> He's found a frozen dinner.</i>

00:41:39.396 --> 00:41:43.967 line:0%
(music)

00:41:43.967 --> 00:41:49.206 line:0%
(music)

00:41:49.206 --> 00:41:50.841 line:0%
<i> It takes the keenest nose</i>

00:41:50.841 --> 00:41:55.112 line:0%
<i> to pick up the scent
 of a carcass in winter.</i>

00:41:55.112 --> 00:42:00.584 line:0%
<i> Wolverines outmatch most
 other animals with this skill.</i>

00:42:00.584 --> 00:42:04.188 line:0%
<i> But then they have to contend
 with each other.</i>

00:42:07.858 --> 00:42:11.795 line:0%
<i> Within minutes,
 the competition arrives.</i>

00:42:11.795 --> 00:42:13.930 line:0%
(music)

00:42:13.930 --> 00:42:20.537 line:0%
(music)

00:42:20.537 --> 00:42:25.242 line:0%
<i> This is when the true wolverine
 nature kicks in to the max.</i>

00:42:25.242 --> 00:42:28.612 line:0%
(music)

00:42:28.612 --> 00:42:34.684 line:0%
(music)

00:42:34.684 --> 00:42:36.720 line:0%
(growling)

00:42:36.720 --> 00:42:42.192 line:0%
(growling)

00:42:42.192 --> 00:42:46.229 line:0%
(music)

00:42:46.229 --> 00:42:52.969 line:0%
(music)

00:42:52.969 --> 00:42:56.973 line:0%
<i> The semi-retractable claws
 come out.</i>

00:42:56.973 --> 00:43:00.476 line:0%
<i> The specialized teeth
 are bared.</i>

00:43:00.476 --> 00:43:02.346 line:0%
<i> It's all-out war.</i>

00:43:05.115 --> 00:43:08.551 line:0%
<i> The defender gets
 the upper claw...</i>

00:43:08.551 --> 00:43:11.521 line:0%
(snarling)

00:43:11.521 --> 00:43:13.757 line:0%
<i> ...and wins his meal back.</i>

00:43:13.757 --> 00:43:15.592 line:0%
(music)

00:43:15.592 --> 00:43:22.365 line:0%
(music)

00:43:22.365 --> 00:43:26.670 line:0%
<i> Powerful jaws break down
 the entire animal,</i>

00:43:26.670 --> 00:43:31.909 line:0%
<i> including hooves,
 teeth and bones.</i>

00:43:33.577 --> 00:43:38.048 line:0%
<i> This is his turf and his food;</i>

00:43:38.048 --> 00:43:41.318 line:0%
<i> food that was supposed
 to be convenient.</i>

00:43:43.754 --> 00:43:49.259 line:0%
<i> But this is deadly Alaska
 where the challenges are epic.</i>

00:43:49.259 --> 00:43:51.328 line:0%
(music)

00:43:51.328 --> 00:43:56.600 line:0%
(music)

00:43:56.600 --> 00:43:58.401 line:0%
<i> Animals like the wolverine</i>

00:43:58.401 --> 00:44:01.905 line:0%
<i> don't just survive
 the tough environment,</i>

00:44:01.905 --> 00:44:05.476 line:0%
<i> they thrive because of it.</i>

